        "explanation": "<p>In the voltage gain formula for a common-emitter amplifier, $A_v = -g_m R_C$, the term $g_m$ represents the <b>transconductance</b> of the transistor. Transconductance is the ratio of the change in collector current to the change in base-emitter voltage, measured in siemens (S).</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
